%~B, since we cannot in general assume that the
%sections $f_j$ in Theorem~B extend to $Y$. In the proof in Section
%\ref{ormbo} we instead construct a complex that extends the Koszul
%complex $(E^f_\bullet, f)$ of $f_j$ and an associated residue current, by using $\nabla_g$-closed
%extensions of $f_j$. 
%\end{remark}








