$0\to\Ok(E_M)\stackrel{g^M}{\to} \ldots\stackrel{g^3}{\to} \Ok(E_2)\stackrel{g^2}{\to} \Ok(E_1)
\stackrel{g^1}{\to} \Ok$
is a  resolution of the sheaf $\Ok/\J_X$ over $\P^N$, where  $E_k$ are
as in Subsection~\ref{lotta}.
The restriction mapping
\begin{equation}\label{sur}
\Ok(\P^N,\Ok(\ell))\to \Ok(X,\Ok(\ell))
\end{equation}
is surjective if $\ell\ge \max_i d_N^i-N$. If $M<N$,
then \eqref{sur} is surjective for all ~$\ell$.
\end{prop}

In particular,  $\kappa\le\max_i d^i_N -N$.
