Let $\phi$ be a global holomorphic section of $\Ok(\ell)\to X$ and let
$\Phi$ be a smooth $\nabla_g$-closed extension of $\phi$ to $\P^N$ as in
Lemma~\ref{ut}.  Notice that $\Phi_N$ is a smooth $(0,N)$-form that takes values in
$\oplus_i \Ok(\ell-d^i_N)$ so by \eqref{pnko} there is a smooth solution to
$\dbar w_N=\Phi_N$ if $\ell-d_N^i\ge -N$ for all $i$. We can then successively find smooth
solutions to  the
equations $\dbar w_k=\Phi_k+g^{k+1}w_{k+1}$ for $k=N-1,\ldots,  1$. Finally we obtain  the
holomorphic section  $\hat\phi=\Phi_0+g^1 w_1$ of $\Ok(\ell)$ over $\P^N$, which,
since $w_1$ is smooth, coincides with $\Phi_0$  on $X$. If $M<N$ no
cohomological obstruction occurs, cf., \eqref{pnko}.
\end{proof}



For $X\subset \P^N$ let $M_X=\C[z_0,\ldots,z_N]/J_X$, where $J_X$ is the homogeneous ideal
associated with $X$, cf., Subsection~\ref{lotta}.  The {\it regularity}
$\reg X$ of $X$,  introduced by Eisenbud and Goto, \cite{EisGot},
is defined as $\max_{i,k}(d_k^i-k)$ for a minimal free resolution
of $M_X$ as in Subsection~\ref{lotta}. %%Example~\ref{arkitekt}.
It follows from Proposition~\ref{extprop} that $\kappa\le\reg X$.
This estimate also follows from  \cite{EisGot}, see  
